## 3. Authentication Flow

### 3.1 Admin (session-based)
```
POST /admin/login { email, password }
  ├─ RateLimitMiddleware.check('login', ip)  → 429 if exceeded
  ├─ DB: SELECT * FROM admin_users WHERE email=? AND is_active=1
  ├─ password_verify(password, hash) — Argon2id
  ├─ On success:
  │    session_regenerate_id(true)
  │    $_SESSION['admin_id'] = id
  │    $_SESSION['role']     = role
  │    Set-Cookie: fg_session (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict)
  │    Set-Cookie: fg_csrf    (non-HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict)
  │    UPDATE admin_users SET last_login_at = NOW()
  │    INSERT INTO audit_log (action='login', actor_id, ip)
  │    return { data: { id, email, role, must_change_pw } }
  └─ On failure → 401 + generic message (never leak "email not found")
```

All `/admin/*` routes pass through `AuthMiddleware`:
- Session valid? → attach `$_SESSION` to request context
- Else → 401 `UNAUTHORIZED`

### 3.2 Public inquiry flow
```
POST /inquiries { name, phone, email?, product_id?, quantity?, inquiry_type, message?, website, cf_token? }
  ├─ Honeypot `website` non-empty → 400
  ├─ RateLimitMiddleware.check('inquiries', ip) → 429
  ├─ Validator.validate(schema) → 422 with field errors
  ├─ (Optional) verify Turnstile token
  ├─ INSERT INTO inquiries (…, status='new')
  ├─ Mailer.notifyOwner(…)
  ├─ INSERT INTO audit_log (action='inquiry_created', entity='inquiry', entity_id)
  └─ 201 { data: { id } }
```

### 3.3 CSRF flow
- Server generates `csrf_token = bin2hex(random_bytes(32))` per session
- Sends as `fg_csrf` cookie (JS-readable, `SameSite=Strict`)
- Client stores in memory on app boot; Axios interceptor injects `X-CSRF-Token`
- `CsrfMiddleware` compares header to session token on all `POST/PATCH/DELETE`
- Mismatch → 403 `FORBIDDEN`

