## 🧭 Why this architecture is agent-agnostic and safe

| Failure mode | How this design prevents it |
|--------------|----------------------------|
| Agent invents architecture mid-task | `04_TRD.md` + `05_Schema.md` are LOCKED; any deviation requires a Change Log entry |
| Agent drifts off-brand | `03_UI_Spec.md` locks colors, fonts, spacing, states at token level |
| Agent forgets Bengali-numeral rule | Repeated in PRD §6, UI Spec §2, TRD, and all 3 agent config files |
| Agent skips error/empty states | `02_AppFlow.md §5` enumerates every required state |
| Agent jumps ahead in scope | `06_Plan.md` is the source of truth for "current work"; pre-flight forces locating the first unchecked step |
| Agent silently skips steps | Update protocol requires `- [x]` + ISO timestamp + commit — a receipt trail in git |
| Agent adds forbidden features | PRD §5 Non-Goals + agent §5 Refusals; both explicit |
| Agent breaks security | TRD §5 lists 15 non-negotiable constraints; agent refuses SQLi-prone patterns |
| Context loss between AI Studio sessions | `06_Plan.md` committed to repo = persistent state; re-attach + bootstrap restores full context |

